<!--Post: 5717--><!--Time: 1107300814-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5717"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 3:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It was proposed in the &#34;Talking to Tom&#34; thread that a new thread topic be started for us site users to post our speculations and suggestions for our own profiles of BTK.  There&#39;s fascinating expert observations in both the Brown and Kelleher profiles.  I&#39;m going to add my 2 cents worth here. <BR> <BR>&#34;BTK&#34;: <BR>&#42; Is a hunter.  He&#39;s familiar with rural areas around Wichita, I&#39;m curious to know if the unsolved rural murders are located near known hunting areas. BTK also enjoys stalking and killing, hunting would give him practice.  He&#39;s also interested in the military and claims to have been in the military,and hunting would give him similar survivalist and hunt/kill thrills. I think he&#39;s an occasional hunter, and doesn&#39;t enjoy shooting as much as stabbing or snaring/strangling animals. <BR>&#42; Is an unusually choosy, and occasionally uncoordinated dresser. He wore an orange shirt and sweater or jacket at the Bright crime scene, these were possibly hunting clothes, or maybe I&#39;m wrong and it was just a 70&#39;s fashion atrocity.  Aside from that he wore a black ski mask, why bother with that if he&#39;s going to kill everyone in the house who could identify him?  BTK likes to accessorize!  I also think he wears the ski mask when he hunts during cold weather, it could be part of his fantasy killer persona.  Normally he tries to blend in and dress in a tidy, casual and almost conservative way &#40;one witness described him wearing a jean jacket and jeans&#41;, but he doesn&#39;t always pull it off, as we see with the orange shirt above. <BR>&#42; Owns alphabet stencils.  The lettering on the cereal box looked to me like it was written by tracing using a stencil. He has used them in the past, but probably bought one recently. <BR>&#42; Draws circles by tracing around a round object, like a glass, a can, a drink coaster, etc..  The cereal box had the letter &#34;T&#34; circled with a black marker, and it looked almost perfectly round, like it was traced around a glass or can or something like that. <BR>&#42; Neat and tidy with his own belongings, but a bit careless with things belonging to other people. <BR>&#42; Uses only black pens and markers to write with. <BR>&#42; Is not spontaneous.  He prefers to plan and prepare for any event or occasion.   <BR>&#42; Has a hispanic mother, and an Anglo father.  <BR>&#42; His mother was Catholic, his father was Protestant. Both parents were regular church goers. When he was young, the family attended his father&#39;s church. His father was very strict.  His father died or walked out when &#34;BTK&#34; was older, and then &#34;BTK&#34; attended a Catholic church with his mother. <BR>&#42; On the job, he liked to give his coworkers the impression that he was smart enough to have gone further with his education than he did.  He likes to give the impression that he left college because the professors weren&#39;t as smart as he was. <BR>&#42; He&#39;s very mechanical.  He can repair an engine if he needs to. <BR>&#42; He&#39;s a stamp collector.  He knows other stamp collectors and may even attend stamp shows. <BR>&#42; His hair style has changed a few times over the years.  Sometimes very short, sometimes longer and not as tidy. <BR>&#42; He walks with a lot of energy in his stride, or at least he did when he was younger.   <BR>&#42; He has a low patience threshold unless he&#39;s waiting for something very important to him. <BR> <BR>That&#39;s what I&#39;ve come up with -- for now. More to come, no doubt! <BR>&#42;   <!--/Text--></td></tr>
