<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6507"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tecno242<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tecno242<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 07, 2005 - 9:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t think he was ever married.  He&#39;s likely to self absorbed to desire a family or attempt to create a &#34;normal&#34; life for himself.  He probably failed, at an early age, on any attempts of a normal relationship.  He would be very controlling in his personal life and would not respond well to rejection.  One rejection of his control was probably enough for him to form a very negative opinion of women and send him deeper into his fantasy world of sexual gratification. <BR> <BR>I do not believe any one event in his life triggered &#34;the monster&#34; to reveal itself.  It could have occured slowly over time, building to the obsession it has become.  If any one event did trigger it, I believe it could have been his fathers death. <BR> <BR>He is certainly internet savy. He probably uses it frequently to satisfy his needs without actually killing.  He knows killing is wrong and he would like to stop, but he does enjoy it.  It&#39;s not the actual act of killing however, but the intense feeling of power over his victims that he craves.  I think this is displayed most in his practice of bringing his victims to the brink of death only to bring them back and repeat.   <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t believe his mother was present as a child.  She either left them or was dead.  His father may have been in the military and exerted a great deal of control over him.  His father may have beat him, but more likely verbally abused him to the point of making him feel worthless and unloved.  If he has siblings, and I don&#39;t believe so, he no longer has any connection with them.  A personality such as his, unable to identify with anyone and completely self absorbed, I think must be created as an only child.  A child with siblings learns early to share and love someone other than themselves or thier parents. <BR> <BR>His father probably died years ago, possibly before the murders began.  Like Michael Jackson, he was probably left with no authority figure to guide him or correct him.  This would also explain why he is so difficult to find, he has no surving relatives of any kind and probably no friends that truly know him.  I would compare his situation to Ed Gein. <BR> <BR>The difference however would be that BTK is quite intelligent and can function normally when in public. <BR> <BR>I believe he has worked the same job for quite some time but was not particulary successful nor a failure.  He probably works a job with little social interaction and not much chance for advancment.  He would be content sliding by.  My guesses for occupations include a security gaurd, data entry position &#40;possibly at the Kansas DMV&#41;, or a local contractor doing odd jobs.  Any of these would allow him to hand pick victims and could provide him with addresses. <BR> <BR>I&#39;d like to add that these are just my personal opinions, so they don&#39;t mean much.   But i would still like to share them. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
