<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6810"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Foxfire<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Foxfire<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 10:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here&#39;s my imagined profile of him: <BR> <BR>I think he is probably 60 to 64 years of age. <BR>I think he may simply have 1/4th or even 1/8th Native American blood which gives him the facial features but not necessarily the coloring. <BR>I think he is currently living alone in a frame house. <BR>He had a long time live-in girlfriend with at least one child, probably a boy, who BTK sort of felt sorry for as it reminded him of himself when he was kid. <BR>The boy grew up and moved out, and then the girlfriend moved out as well eventually because of BTK&#39;s lack of emotional intimacy. <BR>I think he&#39;s not sick so much as feeling his mortality or just &#34;feeling old&#34;. <BR>I don&#39;t believe he was really in law enforcement. Instead I think he picked up a lot of terms and mannerisms from the railroad detective his mother dated as well as railroad personnel. <BR>I don&#39;t think he drinks much if any, any more, if he ever did, but he may still smoke. <BR>He wears both jeans and khaki&#39;s a lot. <BR>He has one medium sized dog that he takes for walks sometimes, but he&#39;s really just using the dog to appear &#34;normal&#34; as he sort of cases places &#34;just in case&#34; he thinks he can ever gain control of another person. <BR>He may drive a P/U truck that is gray or silver. <BR>I think he carries a knife for protection of some sort, but that like somebody else said probably carries a gun when he makes his drops. <BR>I think he becomes really nervous and excited when he makes the drops and that&#39;s it&#39;s a substitute for what he can no longer do -- more than just &#34;for fun&#34; to taunt the police. <BR> <BR>I&#39;ve been having some weird dreams about him as well: <BR> <BR>One time I saw 4 shadowy towers with large birds flying up towards them as if I was seeing through his eyes. The sky was very overcast.  I didn&#39;t know what this meant &#40;if anything&#41;, but I did take the time to look up &#34;four towers and Wichita&#34;.  I came up with the new bridges at West Douglas and Lewis Streets.  I had no idea they existed until then as I don&#39;t live in the state of Kansas and I&#39;ve never been there in my life!  So I&#39;m wondering if he actually lives close to the river &#40;maybe the other side&#41; or if he walks on the riverwalk or the nearby park sometimes. <BR> <BR>Then a few nights later on, I dreamt that he was asking a female victim, &#34;Do you go to church?&#34;  I hear her saying, &#34;Yes.&#34;  He replies, &#34;Good.  Then you know where you&#39;re going after I&#39;m done with you.&#34; <BR> <BR>It&#39;s really, really chilling to me as I really have had true dreams before in the past and told family members or friends, and they have turned out to be true. <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
