neering and the physical sciences. Reference to the X factor. <BR>Believes his poetry can rival Keats, Eliot and Chaucer. Poetry serves to taunt and manipulate the police, media and public rather than demonstrating literary merit. <BR>He did not commit murder before January 1974. <BR>The intended targets in each case was a mother, apart from Kathryn Bright and Nancy Fox. <BR>Sought to resolve his oedipal complex by murdering women who embodied some qualities shared with his mother. <BR>Taunted the Wichita Police Department, the media and the publlic to demonstrate his superior intelligence, to receive attention and recognition as a sadistic serial murderer. <BR>Ended dialogue with the Wichita Police Department and media to ensure freedom. He feared capture. <BR>Between 1979 and 2004 continued to murder. Murdered Vicki Wegerle in 1986. He did not inform the police or media to ensure freedom. <BR>Dialogue re-established in March 2004 after Robert Beattie received publicity for crafting a draft for a book on the BTK Strangler. <BR>He may be divorced and children moved away from home, but the catalyst was Beattie&#39;s book. <BR>The unknown subject is infuriated with the book. He considers Beattie is not qualified or competent to write the book on his career. <BR>Is familiar with the Department of Motor Vehicles, the public library system and several enterprises in the Wichita, Kansas area. <BR>The unknown subject will continue to communicate with the media and the Wichita Police Department.  <BR>He will confirm responsibility for the murder of Kathryn Bright and several unknown murders in the near future.  <BR>It will maintain public interest in his dialogue and elevate his status to one of the most successful serial murderers.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
