<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7672"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Kansasgirl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Kansasgirl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 6:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wichita, Kansas - Air Capital Of The World <BR> <BR>The one thing Wichita is known for. We have Boeing, Raytheon &#40;formerly Beech Aircraft&#41;, Cessna, Bombardier Learjet, and Airbus. Everywhere you turn you find someone who works on planes in some shape or form. Our pool of engineers here is phenomenal. Wichita State University is even known for its engineering department.  <BR> <BR>If you consider most everything that has been said by BTK about himself is false &#40;why believe a man who likes to play games&#41; and look at the community, this is my two cents. <BR> <BR>BTK is an aircraft engineer. He fits into society because he is just like half of Wichita. He did go to WSU - where he received a degree in engineering. He left a note for police in an engineering book! Any lapse in murders is due to the fact he has switched companies. Engineers do not work at the same place for 30 years. They go to Texas to Lockhead Martin, Boeing in Seattle,  or overseas to various aircraft companies. He fits in at any company. He sits in a cubicle next to another guy in a cubicle. <BR> <BR>His murder scenes remind me of an engineer. They are precise, very tidy, and in general, meticulous.  <BR> <BR>I have no idea about childhood frustrations, psychology, etc. I was just looking at the make-up of this community.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
