<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7864"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Raidar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Raidar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 12:49 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->He had a mother who babied him.  She made him feel like she was the only person he needed.  This is where his relationship problems with women came from.  He was very quiet and kept to his self in school,therefore he was teased growing up but was very smart.  He married but then divorced because of how his mother treated his wife.  She was extreamly jealous of the new woman in her sons life.  I think he loved his wife,but i think he feared his mothers rejection.  This is when he turned in to BTK.  He was very angry at his mother for what she had done to his marriage.  He killed out of anger toward her.  He is very clean cut and fits in well everywhere.  He is polite,soft spoken,and calm. He is a very educated man.  I think he works with people&#40;mental health or something of that type.&#41;  Not because he feels remorse for what he did,but rather to figure out why he did it or because he loves to hear the paitents stories of torture and/or grief and tragady they have sufferd.  &#40;Misery loves Company&#41;He did serve in the military.  I think this is where he learned to be unseen and unheard.  He doesnt have a social life,but he does want to be popular and known since that never happened to him in school.  He spends his time watching tv,reading and on his lap top.  He doesnt want to be caught.  He thinks in his mind he wont be a icon anymore,he will be just another SK caught and waiting to meet his maker.  He doesnt live in Wichita anymore,but he still close enough that he doesnt feel threatened.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
